            "costUsd": 0.39064260000000006,
            "finalAnswer": "I now have the complete picture, from the React component down to the roughjs generator calls.\n\n## Trace\n\n**1. React component → `renderStaticScene`**\n\n`StaticCanvas` (`packages/excalidraw/components/canvases/StaticCanvas.tsx`) is the component that actually drives rendering. On every render, its `useEffect` (line 33-81) resizes the canvas and then calls:\n\n```ts\nrenderStaticScene({ canvas, rc: props.rc, scale, elementsMap, allElementsMap, visibleElements, appState, renderConfig }, isRenderThrottlingEnabled())\n```\n\n`renderStaticScene` (in `packages/excalidraw/renderer/staticScene.ts`) either throttles via `renderStaticSceneThrottled` (rAF-throttled) or calls the internal `_renderStaticScene` directly, which iterates `visibleElements` and calls `renderElement(...)` for each one (`packages/excalidraw/renderer/renderElement.ts`).\n\n**2. `renderElement` → obtaining the roughjs shape**\n\nInside `renderElement`, before drawing, it calls `ShapeCache.generateElementShape(element, renderConfig)` — this is a caching layer (`packages/excalidraw/scene/ShapeCache.ts`) backed by a `WeakMap<ExcalidrawElement, ElementShape>`. If a shape is already cached for that element object, it's returned as-is; otherwise it calls the low-level generator `_generateElementShape(element, ShapeCache.rg, ...)` from `packages/excalidraw/scene/Shape.ts` and stores the result in the WeakMap.\n\n**3. `_generateElementShape` → actual roughjs generation**\n\n`_generateElementShape` (`packages/excalidraw/scene/Shape.ts`) switches on `element.type` and calls the roughjs `RoughGenerator` (`generator.rectangle(...)`, `generator.ellipse(...)`, `generator.polygon(...)`, `generator.path(...)`, `generator.linearPath(...)`, `generator.curve(...)`, etc.), passing rough options built by `generateRoughOptions` (stroke, fill, roughness, seed, dash pattern, etc., derived from the element's own properties). This produces a roughjs `Drawable` (or array of `Drawable`s for lines/arrows, including separate arrowhead shapes).\n\n**4. Actually drawing to canvas**\n\nBack in `renderElement`/`drawElementOnCanvas`, the cached shape is fetched again via `ShapeCache.get(element)` and handed to the roughjs canvas instance: `rc.draw(shape)` (`rc` is the `RoughCanvas` passed down from `StaticCanvas` props), which paints the sketchy shape onto the `CanvasRenderingContext2D`.\n\nSo the flow is:\n`StaticCanvas` (React, `useEffect`) → `renderStaticScene`/`_renderStaticScene` (`staticScene.ts`) → `renderElement`/`drawElementOnCanvas` (`renderElement.ts`) → `ShapeCache.generateElementShape`/`ShapeCache.get` (`ShapeCache.ts`, WeakMap cache) → `_generateElementShape` (`Shape.ts`, actual `RoughGenerator` calls) → `rc.draw(shape)`.",
